  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (scvi_n200 + resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) at 0.713. The image-only ResNet50 baseline was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image encoder may be a bottleneck in the multimodal fusion. Config_039 swaps only the image encoder to ViT-L (imagenet_vit_l) while keeping the proven-best RNA encoder (scvi_n200), profile (multiprofile), aggregation (transformer), and fusion (weighted, which outperformed concat by ~2.5pp). This isolates the effect of image representation quality. If ViT-L provides a stronger visual embedding, it could push accuracy above 0.713; if not, we retain 0.713 as our best. This is the highest-value single change to test with one experiment remaining, as it directly extends the winning configuration along the most uncertain axis (image encoder strength) without introducing multiple simultaneous changes."
}

